// `returns_of(target)` takes a runtime `string` naming a fn or method — the same target keying
// `params_of`. A non-`string` operand (here an `int`) is a type mismatch (E0007). What the string
// *names* stays lenient, though: an unknown callable is a runtime `none`, not a static error, since
// a reflection-driven framework generally computes the target rather than writing it out.
// expect: error E0007 at 7:6
// expect: exit 1
echo returns_of(42);
